export const DOCS_CONTENT_MAP: Record<string, string> = {
  "admin/order-settings": "# Admin Order Settings\n\nConfigure global store checkout parameters, default platform processing fees, tax percentage rules, and standard delivery fee structures.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Order Settings](/dashboard/admin/order-settings)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Admin Order Settings](./images/admin-order-settings.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Admin Order Settings page displaying platform processing fee inputs, payment gateway fee settings, tax configuration, and default shipping rates.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Order Settings console lets platform administrators define the financial parameters governing customer checkouts. You can adjust default payment gateway processing fee percentages, configure platform transaction commissions, and manage sitewide tax and delivery defaults.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Set global platform commission rates applied to seller product sales.\n- Configure payment gateway processing fee passing rules (e.g., absorbed by platform vs. charged to buyer).\n- Define default delivery fee recommendations for physical goods.\n- Set GST / sales tax calculation parameters.\n- Enable or disable specific payment gateway channels.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open Order Settings\nNavigate to **Admin Panel > Order Settings** (`/dashboard/admin/order-settings`).\n\n### Step 2: Configure Platform Fee & Tax Rates\n1. Update the **Platform Commission (%)** (e.g., `5.0%`).\n2. Set the **Payment Gateway Processing Fee (%)** (e.g., `2.0%`).\n3. Set standard **GST / Tax Percentage** if applicable.\n\n### Step 3: Save Configuration\nClick **Save Order Settings** to apply changes globally across all future store checkouts.\n\n## Available Order Settings\n\n| Parameter | Function |\n|---|---|\n| **Platform Commission (%)** | Percentage fee deducted from gross sales prior to seller payout. |\n| **Payment Gateway Fee (%)** | Processing surcharge for Razorpay / payment network transactions. |\n| **Default Shipping Fee** | Baseline delivery charge suggested for physical catalog items. |\n| **Tax / GST Rate (%)** | Standard tax rate applied during final customer checkout calculation. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Payment Settlement](./payment-settlement) — View settlements calculated based on these fee rules.\n- [Orders Management](../../products/orders) — Seller-facing view of customer orders.\n",
  "admin/overview": "# Admin Overview & System Settings\n\nThe Admin Panel is the control center for system administrators and staff to configure platform pricing, manage point reward economics, grant VIP Pro subscriptions, and monitor platform health.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Admin Panel](/dashboard/admin)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Admin Panel Overview](./images/admin-overview.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Admin Panel dashboard displaying global platform metrics, plan pricing config cards, point reward rules, VIP Pro grant tools, and affiliate percentage settings.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Admin Overview provides platform-wide control over AnyDM operations. Only authenticated users with superuser or staff permissions can access this section. Administrators can adjust subscription prices, modify referral point reward formulas, manage affiliate commission splits, and oversee user lifecycles.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> The Admin Panel is strictly restricted to platform administrators and staff members.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- View sitewide active creators, total processed DMs, gross platform revenue, and pending KYC applications.\n- Configure global subscription plan pricing (Creator Pro monthly/annual costs).\n- Manage Point Economy rules (e.g., points awarded per referral signup, point redemption exchange rates).\n- Grant sponsored VIP Free Pro access to designated creator accounts.\n- Configure default affiliate commission percentages (e.g., 10.0% revenue share).\n- Access administrative sub-queues: User Management, Verify KYC, Payment Settlements, and Order Settings.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Access the Admin Panel\nNavigate to **Admin Panel** at the bottom of the main sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Configure Subscription & Plan Parameters\n1. In the **Plan & Pricing Settings** card, adjust the standard monthly subscription cost for Creator Pro.\n2. Click **Save Pricing Config**.\n\n### Step 3: Configure Referral Point Rules\n1. In the **Point Economy Rules** section, define how many points are awarded for peer referrals and social follow actions.\n2. Set the redemption exchange rate (default: 100 points = 1 Month Pro Extension).\n3. Click **Update Point Rules**.\n\n### Step 4: Grant VIP Creator Pro\n1. Under **VIP Free Pro Grant**, search for a creator's email or username.\n2. Select the validity duration (e.g., 3 months, 6 months, 12 months).\n3. Click **Grant VIP Access**.\n\n## Available Admin Controls & System Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Pro Monthly Price** | Global price charged for monthly Creator Pro subscriptions (Default: ₹499). |\n| **Referral Signup Points** | Points credited to a user when a referred friend joins (Default: 50 pts). |\n| **Pro Extension Cost** | Points required to redeem 1 month of Free Pro (Default: 100 pts). |\n| **VIP Affiliate Split** | Percentage revenue share paid to VIP creators on subscription checkouts (Default: 10.0%). |\n| **Minimum Payout** | Minimum accumulated creator balance required to submit a bank withdrawal (Default: ₹500). |\n| **Superuser Privileges** | System access controls for user management, KYC approvals, and financial payouts. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [User Management](./users) — Inspect and manage registered users, points, and permissions.\n- [Verify KYC Queue](./verify-kyc) — Review seller identity documents.\n- [Payment Settlement](./payment-settlement) — Process seller and affiliate bank payouts.\n- [Admin Reference Spec](./spec) — Full architectural documentation on membership rules and token economics.\n",
  "admin/payment-settlement": "# Admin Payment Settlement\n\nProcess seller payout transfers, review creator withdrawal requests, monitor transaction fees, and log bank settlement disbursements.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Payment Settlement](/dashboard/admin/payment-settlement)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Admin Payment Settlement Dashboard](./images/admin-payment-settlement.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Payment Settlement dashboard displaying pending payout requests table, disbursement amounts, bank IFSC routing, batch settlement trigger, and transaction status chips.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Payment Settlement console handles the disbursement of funds from platform escrow to sellers and affiliate creators. Administrators can review pending payouts, confirm seller KYC compliance, initiate batch transfers, and mark transactions as completed.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- View all pending seller earnings and creator affiliate payout requests.\n- Verify seller KYC verification status and bank details prior to disbursement.\n- Filter payouts by status (`Pending`, `Processing`, `Completed`, `Failed`).\n- Execute individual or batch payout transfers via bank integration or manual NEFT/IMPS entry.\n- Export payout settlement logs for financial auditing.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open Payment Settlement\nNavigate to **Admin Panel > Payment Settlement** (`/dashboard/admin/payment-settlement`).\n\n### Step 2: Inspect Pending Payouts\n1. Review the list of requested withdrawals.\n2. Confirm the seller's KYC status is marked `APPROVED`.\n3. Check gross sales amount, platform commission deductions, and net payout payable.\n\n### Step 3: Process Transfer\n1. Initiate the bank transfer using the listed bank account and IFSC.\n2. Enter the bank transaction reference number (UTR).\n3. Click **Mark as Settled**. The seller's pending balance will update to cleared.\n\n## Settlement Data Fields\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Seller / Creator** | Account name and email of the payee. |\n| **Gross Sales / Commission** | Total earnings before platform fees. |\n| **Net Payable Amount** | Exact monetary sum to be transferred to the seller. |\n| **Bank Account & IFSC** | Receiving bank destination information. |\n| **UTR / Reference No.** | Bank transaction reference tracking code entered upon completion. |\n| **Settlement Status** | `PENDING`, `PROCESSING`, `SETTLED`, or `REJECTED`. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Verify KYC Queue](./verify-kyc) — Ensure sellers are verified before settling funds.\n- [Creator Hub](../../creator) — User portal where creators submit withdrawal requests.\n- [Order Settings](./order-settings) — Configure platform commission rates.\n",
  "admin/spec": "# Admin Reference Specification\n\nComprehensive technical specification for membership plans, point rewards, VIP Free Pro lifecycle, affiliate commission economics, and automated settlement rules.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Admin Reference Docs](/dashboard/admin/docs)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Admin Reference Spec](./images/admin-docs-spec.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Admin Reference Documentation view displaying system architecture diagrams, token rules, affiliate lifecycle formulas, and raw markdown export controls.\n\n## Overview\n\nThis specification documents the platform mechanics, membership models, reward calculations, and financial workflows that govern the AnyDM operating system. It acts as the definitive reference manual for administrators and support leads.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Review complete specifications for Free Trial, Creator Pro, and VIP Pro membership tiers.\n- Inspect exact point distribution algorithms for user referrals and social follow actions.\n- Review mathematical formulas for affiliate commission splits and minimum payout thresholds.\n- Copy the raw markdown specification to your clipboard for external reference or compliance audits.\n- Jump directly into Admin Settings to adjust these parameters.\n\n## System Architecture & Model Specifications\n\n### 1. Membership Plan Models\n\n| Plan Tier | Pricing | DM Automations | Master AI Access | Duration |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Free / Trial Tier** | ₹0 | Standard rate limits (200 DMs/hr) | Custom API key required | 14 Days default |\n| **Creator Pro Tier** | ₹499 / mo | Unlimited fast triggers | Built-in Master AI token | Monthly / Annual |\n| **Creator VIP Pro** | ₹0 (Sponsored) | Unlimited fast triggers | Built-in Master AI token | 1–24 Months configurable |\n\n### 2. Point Economy Rules\n\n- **Referral Inbound**: When an existing user's referral code is used during signup, the referrer receives **+50 Points**.\n- **Social Follow Task**: Following `@anydm.in` on Instagram awards **+10 Points** once per account upon automated verification.\n- **Redemption**: **100 Points = 30 Days Free Pro Subscription Extension**.\n\n### 3. VIP Creator Affiliate Economics\n\n- **Commission Split**: Approved VIP creators earn **10.0% recurring revenue share** on all paid subscription checkouts generated through their affiliate tracking code.\n- **Minimum Withdrawal**: Payout requests require a minimum cleared balance of **₹500**.\n- **Compliance Lock**: All payouts strictly require an **APPROVED** Seller KYC document status.\n\n## How to Export\n\n1. Open **Admin Reference Docs** (`/dashboard/admin/docs`).\n2. Click the **Copy Raw .MD** button in the header.\n3. The complete system specification markdown is copied to your clipboard.\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Admin Overview](./overview) — Modify global system pricing and points.\n- [Verify KYC Queue](./verify-kyc) — Manage seller document verification.\n- [Payment Settlement](./payment-settlement) — Execute seller and creator bank payouts.\n",
  "admin/users": "# Admin User Management\n\nInspect registered creator accounts, adjust reward points, grant VIP Pro access, toggle staff privileges, and troubleshoot user issues.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open User Management](/dashboard/admin/users)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Admin User Management Table](./images/admin-users.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Admin User Management table showing user list, plan badges, point balances, connected Instagram accounts, superuser flags, and action menus.\n\n## Overview\n\nUser Management gives administrators complete visibility over platform accounts. Staff can search for specific users, audit their subscription status and connected Instagram handles, manually credit or debit reward points, and grant VIP privileges.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Search and filter all registered AnyDM users by name, email, or Instagram username.\n- Inspect account plan details (`Free Trial`, `Creator Pro`, `VIP Pro`, `Expired`).\n- View total points balance and referral statistics per user.\n- Manually adjust a user's point balance or extend their subscription validity period.\n- Toggle superuser or staff permissions for administrative staff.\n- Deactivate or suspend problematic accounts.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Search for a User\n1. Navigate to **Admin Panel > Users** (`/dashboard/admin/users`).\n2. Type the user's email, name, or Instagram handle into the search box.\n\n### Step 2: Edit Account Permissions & Points\n1. Click the **Edit / Actions** button on the target user's row.\n2. Modify user points, subscription tier, or staff status in the modal.\n3. Click **Save User Changes**.\n\n## Available User Attributes\n\n| Attribute | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **User Identity** | Full name, email address, and avatar. |\n| **Plan Tier** | Active subscription tier (`Trial`, `Pro`, `VIP Pro`). |\n| **Points Balance** | Current unspent reward points. |\n| **Connected IG Accounts** | Total Instagram professional handles linked by this user. |\n| **Staff / Superuser** | Administrative permission flags. |\n| **Joined Date** | Timestamp of initial platform registration. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Admin Overview](./overview) — System-wide settings and plan configurations.\n- [Verify KYC Queue](./verify-kyc) — Review KYC verification status for users.\n",
  "admin/verify-kyc": "# Admin Verify KYC Queue\n\nReview submitted Seller KYC applications, verify PAN and bank document details, and approve or reject seller payout capabilities.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Verify KYC Queue](/dashboard/admin/verify-kyc)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Admin KYC Verification Queue](./images/admin-verify-kyc.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Admin KYC verification queue showing pending verification cards, applicant PAN and Aadhaar records, bank details, approve button, and rejection dialog.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Verify KYC Queue ensures regulatory compliance by allowing administrators to review seller tax identifiers and bank account information. Approving a KYC application unlocks automated payout settlements and creator withdrawals for that seller.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- View all pending, approved, and rejected KYC applications.\n- Inspect applicant full names, PAN numbers, Aadhaar numbers, and bank account/IFSC data.\n- Validate matching details against tax and banking records.\n- Approve verified applications with a single click.\n- Reject non-compliant or mismatched applications with specific feedback reasons for the user.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Filter Pending Applications\n1. Open **Admin Panel > Verify KYC** (`/dashboard/admin/verify-kyc`).\n2. Select the **Pending Review** filter tab to inspect newly submitted applications.\n\n### Step 2: Review Submitted Data\n1. Review the legal name against the provided PAN and Aadhaar numbers.\n2. Confirm the bank account number format and IFSC branch code.\n\n### Step 3: Approve or Reject\n- **To Approve**: Click **Approve KYC**. The user's status updates immediately to `APPROVED`, enabling their payout settlements.\n- **To Reject**: Click **Reject**, enter the specific rejection reason (e.g., *\"PAN name does not match bank account holder name\"*), and confirm. The user will receive instructions to resubmit.\n\n## KYC Verification Fields\n\n| Field | Check Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| **Applicant Name** | Must match PAN card and official bank account holder records. |\n| **PAN Number** | 10-character alphanumeric Indian tax identifier. |\n| **Aadhaar Number** | 12-digit Indian national identity number. |\n| **Bank Account & IFSC** | Valid receiving bank account number and branch routing code. |\n| **Review Actions** | `Approve` (Grants payout capabilities) or `Reject` (With feedback reason). |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Seller KYC Settings](../../settings/kyc) — The user-facing KYC submission form.\n- [Payment Settlement](./payment-settlement) — Process bank payouts for approved sellers.\n",
  "automations/builder": "# Visual Flow Builder\n\nThe Visual Flow Builder is an interactive node-based canvas for designing customized conversation flows, trigger conditions, multi-message DM sequences, and public comment replies.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Flow Builder](/dashboard/automations)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Visual Flow Builder Canvas](./images/automations-builder.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Visual Flow Builder canvas showing Trigger, Condition, and Action nodes connected by workflow arrows, with side inspection panels and interactive mobile chat preview.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Visual Flow Builder provides a drag-and-drop workspace where creators construct complex marketing funnels visually. You can define exact keyword conditions, link workflows to specific Instagram posts or reels via the Instagram Media Picker, customize DM formats (Plain Text, Quick Replies, Generic Carousels, Button Templates), and preview simulated user interactions live.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Add and connect **Trigger**, **Condition**, and **Action** nodes on an infinite canvas.\n- Select specific Instagram media items (Reels, Posts) or apply rules across all posts.\n- Configure keyword matching filters with case-insensitive logic.\n- Design rich Instagram DM messages: text messages, button links, quick reply pills, and product carousels.\n- Set randomized public comment replies to increase natural engagement and avoid spam detection.\n- Simulate and test the full conversational experience in the live interactive Mobile Preview panel.\n- Save, validate, and publish workflows directly to your live Instagram profile.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Set the Trigger Node\n1. Click on the **Trigger Node** on the canvas.\n2. In the right-hand properties sidebar, select the trigger source:\n   - *User comments on post*\n   - *User sends direct message*\n   - *User clicks welcome icebreaker*\n3. If targeting specific content, click **Select Media** to open the **Instagram Media Picker** and choose a post or reel.\n\n### Step 2: Define Keyword Conditions\n1. Click the **Condition Node** connected to your trigger.\n2. Enter trigger keywords separated by commas (e.g., `BUY, DISCOUNT, LINK, PRICE`).\n3. Set match mode to *Contains any keyword* or *Exact keyword*.\n\n### Step 3: Configure Response Actions\n1. Click the **Action Node**.\n2. Select your **DM Format**:\n   - **Text**: Standard direct message with emoji and personalization placeholders.\n   - **Buttons / Quick Replies**: Direct messages with interactive CTA buttons linking to your storefront or checkout.\n   - **Generic Template / Carousel**: Multi-card swipeable product cards.\n3. Configure optional **Public Comment Reply**: Enter multiple variations (e.g., *\"Check your DM! 📩\"*, *\"Sent you the link in messages! ✨\"*). The system will cycle through them automatically.\n\n### Step 4: Preview and Save\n1. Test your conversation in the right-side **Interactive Chat Simulator**.\n2. Click **Save & Publish Flow** in the top bar.\n\n> **Video tutorial placeholder**\n>\n> Add a video walkthrough demonstrating how to create a high-converting Comment-to-DM automated funnel using the Visual Flow Builder.\n\n## Node Types & Configuration\n\n| Node Type | Purpose & Options |\n|---|---|\n| **Trigger Node** | Defines the entry event: Comment on Post/Reel, Inbound DM, Story Tag, or Welcome Icebreaker. Includes media picker. |\n| **Condition Node** | Evaluates rules such as required keywords, user follow status, or engagement filters. |\n| **Action Node** | Dispatches output actions: sends Instagram Direct Message, fires public comment reply, or sets customer lead tag. |\n| **DM Formats** | Supports Plain Text, Quick Reply Buttons, Button Templates (URL/Postback), and Generic Multi-Card Carousels. |\n| **Live Simulator** | Interactive real-time phone emulator for testing user taps and message delivery before publishing. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Automations Catalog](./catalog) — Manage, toggle, and view analytics for all published flows.\n- [Product Catalog](../products/catalog) — Integrate direct product links into button templates.\n- [Instagram Post Scheduler](../schedule) — Coordinate automated reply rules with scheduled reel launches.\n",
  "automations/catalog": "# Automations Catalog\n\nThe Automations Catalog is your dashboard for creating, managing, activating, and monitoring automated Instagram DM and comment response rules.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Automations](/dashboard/automation)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Automations Catalog](./images/automations-catalog.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Automations Catalog showing active and disabled automation cards, trigger event tags, trigger keyword chips, execution counters, and status toggles.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM Automations allow creators and brands to respond instantly to Instagram comments, direct messages, story mentions, and questions. When followers comment specific keywords (like \"PRICE\", \"LINK\", or \"BUY\") on your posts or reels, AnyDM automatically replies in the comments and delivers a customized direct message with purchase links.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- View all configured automation rules with real-time status (`Active`, `Disabled`, `Completed`).\n- Create new automation workflows from scratch or pre-built templates.\n- Toggle automations active or inactive with a single switch.\n- Filter automations by status (`All`, `Active`, `Disabled`).\n- Switch between Grid and List display modes.\n- Track execution counts and follower growth metrics generated by each rule.\n- Set scheduled start and end expiration dates for time-sensitive marketing campaigns.\n- Open the visual flow builder to edit rule logic and message sequences.\n- Delete obsolete automation rules.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Browse Existing Automations\n1. Open **Automations** from the sidebar.\n2. Review your active rules, their trigger events (Comment Keywords, Direct Message, Welcome Icebreaker, or Chat Menu), and execution counts.\n\n### Step 2: Create a New Automation\n1. Click **+ New Automation** in the top right.\n2. Select whether to create a Comment-to-DM rule, Post Share reply, Story Mention flow, or Welcome profile flow.\n3. This opens the **Visual Flow Builder** to configure trigger keywords and action responses.\n\n### Step 3: Manage Rule Status\n- Use the status toggle button on any automation card to quickly pause or activate the flow.\n- Click the **Pencil / Edit** icon to modify nodes in the visual builder.\n- Click the **Trash** icon to remove the automation.\n\n## Supported Automation Trigger Types\n\n| Trigger Type | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Comment Automation** | Triggers when a user comments on any post or a specific post, with optional keyword filters. |\n| **Direct Message Trigger** | Triggers when an inbound direct message containing specific keywords is received. |\n| **Welcome Message Flow** | Triggers when a new customer opens chat and clicks a suggested icebreaker question. |\n| **Persistent Menu Flow** | Triggers when a customer selects a persistent menu option inside the Instagram chat composer. |\n| **Story Mention Flow** | Triggers when a user tags your Instagram account in their story. |\n| **Post Share Flow** | Triggers when a user shares your post or reel into direct messages. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Visual Flow Builder](./builder) — Drag-and-drop canvas for designing multi-step message logic.\n- [Product Auto-Replies](../products/replies) — Manage automated responses specifically linked to catalog items.\n- [Connected Accounts](../settings/accounts) — Ensure your Instagram account is connected to process webhooks.\n",
  "bio/analytics": "# Bio Analytics & QR Code\n\nTrack visitor engagement, monitor page views and link click rates, and generate branded QR codes for offline customer acquisition.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Link-in-Bio Analytics](/dashboard/bio)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Bio Analytics & QR Modal](./images/bio-analytics.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Link-in-Bio Analytics tab with total page views, link clicks, redirect hits metrics, and the high-resolution QR code modal with download options.\n\n## Overview\n\nBio Analytics gives you clear insights into how effectively your bio profile converts Instagram followers into active link clicks and customers. The built-in QR Code Generator creates high-resolution scan codes suitable for packaging, flyers, pop-up stores, and business cards.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- View aggregate page visits and unique visitor counts.\n- Track total link clicks across all active blocks.\n- Inspect total successful Smart Redirect rule executions.\n- Monitor active vs. total block capacity.\n- Generate and download dynamic QR codes directly linked to your public bio URL.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Review Analytics\n1. Navigate to the **Analytics** tab in the Link-in-Bio dashboard.\n2. Review the top KPI cards:\n   - **Total Views**: Visitor page loads on your public profile.\n   - **Total Clicks**: Outbound interactions on your links and product cards.\n   - **Redirect Hits**: Successful promo link searches.\n   - **Active Blocks**: Count of currently published blocks.\n\n### Step 2: Generate and Download QR Code\n1. Click the **QR Code** button in the top action bar.\n2. A high-resolution QR code is rendered for your profile URL.\n3. Click **Download PNG** to save the image to your computer for marketing collateral.\n\n## Metrics Breakdown\n\n| Metric | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Views Count** | Total times your public bio page was loaded by visitors. |\n| **Clicks Count** | Total clicks across all interactive link blocks and product cards. |\n| **Redirect Hits** | Total instances where visitors resolved a Reel or promo link via the Smart Input. |\n| **Click-Through Rate (CTR)** | Ratio of total clicks to total page views. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Bio Blocks & Links](./blocks) — Individual block click tracking.\n- [Smart Redirects](./redirects) — Track campaign-specific redirect rule hits.\n",
  "bio/blocks": "# Bio Blocks & Links\n\nBio Blocks are the core interactive elements displayed on your Link-in-Bio page, including custom web links, featured products, embedded media, and contact triggers.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Link-in-Bio](/dashboard/bio)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Bio Blocks Management](./images/bio-blocks.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Link-in-Bio Blocks tab showing list of active blocks, drag-and-drop handles, visibility toggles, and block creation modal.\n\n## Overview\n\nBlocks allow you to organize and present your content hierarchically. You can highlight your latest YouTube video, promote special discount links, showcase e-commerce product cards, or collect newsletter signups directly within your bio page.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Add new link blocks, product cards, headers, and media items.\n- Drag and drop or use move buttons to reorder blocks in real time.\n- Toggle block visibility on or off without deleting the block.\n- Edit block titles, subtitles, target URLs, and thumbnail media.\n- Track individual click counts per block.\n- Delete obsolete blocks.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Add a New Block\n1. Navigate to the **Blocks** tab in the Link-in-Bio editor.\n2. Click **+ Add Block**.\n3. Select the block type (Link, Product, Header, Media).\n4. Enter the **Title**, optional **Subtitle**, and the destination **URL**.\n5. Upload an optional thumbnail icon or media file.\n6. Click **Save Block**.\n\n### Step 2: Reorder Your Blocks\n- Hover over any block card and click the grab handle to drag it up or down.\n- Alternatively, use the **Move Up** and **Move Down** arrow controls.\n- Changes are instantly updated on the live preview simulator and public URL.\n\n### Step 3: Manage Block Visibility\n- Use the **Eye / Eye Off** toggle on any block card to temporarily hide or show it.\n\n## Available Block Options\n\n| Field / Action | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Block Type** | Type of block: standard link card, product highlight, heading, or media container. |\n| **Title** | Primary text displayed on the link card. |\n| **Subtitle** | Secondary supportive text or promo code description. |\n| **Destination URL** | External link or internal shop destination opened upon click. |\n| **Media / Icon** | Thumbnail image or icon uploaded to accompany the link. |\n| **Active Switch** | Toggle to show or hide the block from public visitors. |\n| **Click Counter** | Total recorded visitor clicks on this specific block. |\n| **Delete Action** | Permanently removes the block from your page. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Themes & Styling](./styling) — Adjust the visual design and card borders of your blocks.\n- [Smart Redirects](./redirects) — Route incoming visitors directly to specific blocks.\n",
  "bio": "# Link-in-Bio Overview\n\nThe Link-in-Bio feature allows you to build and host a high-converting, mobile-optimized creator profile page with custom links, product showcase cards, social channels, and intelligent URL redirection.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Link-in-Bio](/dashboard/bio)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Link-in-Bio Builder](./images/bio-overview.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Link-in-Bio editor interface showing the live responsive device simulator, navigation tabs, and page configuration settings.\n\n## Overview\n\nYour AnyDM Link-in-Bio serves as the single public link for your Instagram bio (e.g., `yourdomain.com/@username`). It converts social traffic into customers by displaying active product catalogs, lead capture forms, external links, social handles, and an interactive Reel promo resolver.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Customize your public username slug and verify real-time handle availability.\n- Edit your public display title, biographical description, and avatar profile photo.\n- Preview your bio page live across Mobile, Tablet, and Desktop device frames.\n- Toggle page publishing status (Online / Draft).\n- Share or copy your public profile URL with a single click.\n- Download customized QR codes for offline marketing and print materials.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open Link-in-Bio Editor\nNavigate to **Link-in-Bio** from the main sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Configure Your Public Identity\n1. In the top profile bar or **Settings** tab, enter your desired public **Username**.\n2. Wait for the real-time availability check to show `Available`.\n3. Set your **Display Title** and enter a compelling **Bio description**.\n4. Upload your avatar photo and header cover banner.\n\n### Step 3: Preview and Publish\n1. Use the device toggle buttons (`Mobile`, `Tablet`, `Desktop`) above the phone simulator to preview how your profile renders.\n2. Click **Save Changes** in the bottom bar.\n3. Click **Copy Link** to paste into your Instagram bio.\n\n## Available Options\n\n| Option / Setting | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Username Handle** | Your unique public URL slug (`/@username`). |\n| **Profile Title** | Main display name shown at the top of your bio page. |\n| **Bio Description** | Short summary or tagline introducing your brand. |\n| **Profile Photo (Avatar)** | High-resolution circular profile image. |\n| **Banner Image** | Top header cover image for your bio profile. |\n| **Publish Status** | Toggle your bio page live or hidden from public access. |\n| **Device Simulator** | Switch between Mobile (375px), Tablet (640px), and Desktop (100%) views. |\n| **Copy Bio Link** | Copies your public link directly to the clipboard. |\n| **QR Code Generator** | Generates high-resolution QR codes pointing to your bio page. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Blocks & Links](./blocks) — Add clickable link cards, product showcases, and media blocks.\n- [Themes & Styling](./styling) — Customize colors, background overlays, and typography.\n- [Smart Redirects](./redirects) — Route Instagram reel keywords directly to specific destinations.\n- [Bio Analytics](./analytics) — Track visitor views, click-through rates, and link performance.\n",
  "bio/redirects": "# Smart Reel & URL Redirects\n\nSmart Redirects allow creators to link Instagram Reels, post captions, and promotional short-codes directly to specific products, external links, or bio blocks through an intelligent URL resolver.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Smart Redirects](/dashboard/bio)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Smart Redirects Configuration](./images/bio-redirects.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Smart Redirects tab showing active redirection rules, trigger keywords/URLs, destination mappings, hit counters, and the live rule test simulator.\n\n## Overview\n\nWhen creators tell their followers *\"Link in bio to buy!\"* or share specific short URLs in captions and reels, visitors can paste or click the link into the Smart Input bar on your bio page. The Smart Redirect engine instantly resolves the link and forwards the user directly to the exact product or page.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Enable or disable the interactive Smart Input bar on your public bio page.\n- Create keyword or URL match rules (Exact Match or Contains Match).\n- Route matches to multiple destination types: external URLs, specific product items, or bio blocks.\n- Test routing rules in real time using the built-in test runner.\n- Track total hits and traffic redirection count per rule.\n- Customize the input placeholder, title, and button text displayed to visitors.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Enable Smart Redirects\n1. Go to the **Redirects** tab in the Link-in-Bio editor.\n2. Ensure the **Enable Smart Redirect Input** toggle is switched ON.\n3. Customize the **Input Title** (e.g., *\"Have a Reel or Promo Link?\"*), **Placeholder**, and **Button Text** (e.g., *\"Get Link\"*).\n\n### Step 2: Create a Redirect Rule\n1. Click **+ Add Redirect Rule**.\n2. Set a descriptive **Rule Title** (e.g., *\"Summer Dress Reel #42\"*).\n3. Enter the **Input Match URL or Keyword** (e.g., `reel-summer-dress` or Instagram reel permalink).\n4. Choose the **Match Type** (`Exact Match` or `Contains`).\n5. Select the **Destination Type** (`External Link`, `Product`, or `Block`).\n6. Enter or select the destination target and click **Save Rule**.\n\n### Step 3: Test the Rule\n1. Locate your rule in the list.\n2. Click the **Test Rule** button.\n3. Verify that the test runner confirms a successful match and shows the resolved destination.\n\n> **Video tutorial placeholder**\n>\n> Add a short video demonstrating how to set up a Reel promo redirect and test it on the live bio page.\n\n## Available Rule Options\n\n| Option / Field | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Smart Redirect Switch** | Master toggle to show or hide the link resolver search box on your bio page. |\n| **Input Title** | Heading above the input box guiding the visitor. |\n| **Placeholder Text** | Placeholder prompt inside the search box. |\n| **Rule Title** | Internal name for organizing your marketing campaigns. |\n| **Match Keyword / URL** | Text or link pattern entered by the visitor. |\n| **Match Type** | `Exact` (strict string comparison) or `Contains` (substring matching). |\n| **Destination Value** | Target URL or product slug to forward the visitor to. |\n| **Hits Counter** | Number of times visitors successfully triggered this redirect rule. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Link-in-Bio Overview](./) — Public bio page setup.\n- [Product Catalog](../products/catalog) — Link redirect destinations to your store products.\n",
  "bio/social": "# Bio Social Accounts\n\nConnect and showcase your social channels, community groups, and streaming profiles directly on your Link-in-Bio page.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Social Settings](/dashboard/bio)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Bio Social Accounts](./images/bio-social.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Link-in-Bio Social tab showing supported platform network icons, custom social channel adder, display mode options, and handle visibility switches.\n\n## Overview\n\nSocial Accounts let your visitors connect with you across all platforms from one central hub. You can display official brand icons for major social networks, add custom links with dedicated icons, and choose where and how icons appear on your bio page.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Add official profile links for top networks: Instagram, YouTube, X (Twitter), TikTok, WhatsApp, LinkedIn, GitHub, Spotify, Facebook, Twitch, Discord, Telegram, and Pinterest.\n- Create custom channels with custom labels and icons.\n- Toggle between display layouts (e.g., top header icon bar or dedicated link cards).\n- Show or hide platform usernames/handles next to icons.\n- Reorder your social channels.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Add Social Platforms\n1. Open the **Social** tab in the Link-in-Bio dashboard.\n2. Select a platform from the popular network list or click **+ Add Custom Social**.\n3. Enter your handle or direct profile URL (e.g., `https://instagram.com/yourhandle`).\n4. Click **Save**.\n\n### Step 2: Configure Display Settings\n1. Set the **Display Mode** to position icons at the top of your profile or embedded among your blocks.\n2. Toggle **Show Social Usernames** if you want your handles visible beside each network icon.\n\n### Step 3: Save and Verify\nClick **Save Settings** in the bottom bar and verify the appearance on the device simulator.\n\n## Supported Social Platforms\n\n| Platform | Recommended Link Format |\n|---|---|\n| **Instagram** | `https://instagram.com/username` |\n| **YouTube** | `https://youtube.com/@channel` |\n| **X (Twitter)** | `https://x.com/username` |\n| **WhatsApp** | `https://wa.me/phonenumber` |\n| **TikTok** | `https://tiktok.com/@username` |\n| **LinkedIn** | `https://linkedin.com/in/profile` |\n| **Spotify** | `https://open.spotify.com/artist/id` |\n| **Discord** | `https://discord.gg/invitecode` |\n| **Telegram** | `https://t.me/channelname` |\n| **GitHub** | `https://github.com/username` |\n| **Custom Link** | Any valid web URL with a custom icon and label |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Link-in-Bio Overview](./) — General profile layout and preview.\n- [Connected Accounts](../settings/accounts) — Instagram API integration for your AnyDM workspace.\n",
  "bio/styling": "# Bio Themes & Styling\n\nCustomize the visual aesthetics, background palettes, glassmorphic themes, and typography of your Link-in-Bio profile.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Link-in-Bio Styling](/dashboard/bio)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Bio Styling Editor](./images/bio-styling.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Link-in-Bio Styling tab displaying theme presets, custom background color pickers, image background uploaders, and overlay controls.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Styling engine lets creators match their bio page to their unique branding. Choose from pre-designed aesthetic themes or build a custom style using background gradients, custom wallpaper photos, dark/light overlays, and contrasting font colors.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Select from built-in theme presets including *Glass Monochrome*, *Minimal*, *Creator*, *Dark Glass*, *Gradient Glow*, *Cyber Neon*, *Sunset Warmth*, *Clean White*, and *Luxury Gold*.\n- Choose custom background modes: Solid Colors, Preset Gradients, or Custom Image Wallpapers.\n- Adjust background overlay shading (*Dark*, *Heavy*, *Light*) for optimal legibility.\n- Customize primary and secondary text colors.\n- Upload high-resolution cover banners and avatar images.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Select a Theme Preset\n1. In the Link-in-Bio editor, click on the **Styling** tab.\n2. Browse through the available theme cards and click any preset to apply it immediately to the preview simulator.\n\n### Step 2: Customize Background\n1. Under **Background Type**, choose **Preset**, **Custom Color**, or **Image**.\n2. If selecting **Image**, click **Upload Background Image** and choose an image from your device.\n3. Select an overlay intensity (*Dark*, *Heavy*, or *Light*) to ensure text remains crisp and readable over background imagery.\n\n### Step 3: Save Your Style\n1. Review the live simulated render in the right-hand preview panel.\n2. Click **Save Settings** to push changes to your public page.\n\n## Available Theme Presets\n\n| Theme Preset | Visual Style |\n|---|---|\n| **Glass Monochrome** | Sleek charcoal glassmorphism with subtle borders. |\n| **Minimal** | Ultra-clean dark zinc with understated typography. |\n| **Creator** | Deep amethyst purple with radial glow effects. |\n| **Dark Glass** | Navy slate glass container with subtle blue accents. |\n| **Gradient Glow** | Vibrant pink, purple, and indigo neon gradient. |\n| **Cyber Neon** | High-contrast deep cyan with futuristic borders. |\n| **Sunset Warmth** | Amber to rose gradient with warm undertones. |\n| **Clean White** | Bright daylight palette with crisp light card borders. |\n| **Luxury Gold** | Rich metallic gold accents over midnight black. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Link-in-Bio Overview](./) — General profile settings and live preview controls.\n- [Bio Blocks & Links](./blocks) — The interactive cards styled by your theme.\n",
  "creator": "# Creator Hub\n\nThe Creator Hub is an exclusive portal for approved VIP Creators to track revenue sharing, manage affiliate cash commissions, and submit payout withdrawal requests.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Creator Hub](/dashboard/creator)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Creator Hub Dashboard](./images/creator-overview.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Creator Hub dashboard displaying Total Earnings, Available Payout Balance, Pending Commission, 10% Revenue Share metric, and Bank Settlement withdrawal action.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM Creator VIPs earn recurring cash commissions by referring paying subscribers and generating storefront sales. The Creator Hub tracks real-time affiliate earnings, shows payout settlement eligibility, and processes transfers directly to your verified bank account.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The Creator Hub is visible to users with an active Creator VIP or Affiliate partner status.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Track financial balances: **Total Lifetime Earnings**, **Available for Payout**, and **Pending Balance**.\n- Monitor affiliate commission conversion rates (10% standard revenue-share on referred subscription payments).\n- Request direct bank payout settlements once the minimum payout threshold (₹500) is reached.\n- Review historical transaction and payout records.\n- Verify your Seller KYC status to ensure uninterrupted bank settlements.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Access the Creator Hub\nNavigate to **Creator Hub** from the main sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Track Commission Earnings\nReview the top metric cards:\n- **Available Balance**: Cash ready to be withdrawn to your bank.\n- **Pending Balance**: Commission currently in the clearing period.\n- **Referred Pro Conversions**: Total paid subscribers attributed to your affiliate code.\n\n### Step 3: Request a Payout Withdrawal\n1. Once your available balance exceeds **₹500**, click the **Request Payout** button.\n2. Confirm your verified bank account details (managed in Seller KYC).\n3. Click **Submit Withdrawal Request**. Payouts are reviewed and settled by the finance team.\n\n## Creator Program Parameters & Payout Rules\n\n| Parameter | Value / Policy |\n|---|---|\n| **Commission Rate** | 10.0% recurring revenue share on referred paid subscriptions. |\n| **Minimum Payout** | ₹500 minimum balance required to submit a withdrawal request. |\n| **Settlement Method** | Direct Bank Transfer (NEFT / IMPS) or verified UPI ID. |\n| **KYC Requirement** | Approved Seller KYC (PAN + Bank Account) is mandatory before funds are disbursed. |\n| **Clearing Period** | Standard 7-day dispute window before pending funds become available for withdrawal. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Seller KYC Settings](../settings/kyc) — Complete identity and bank account verification for payouts.\n- [Refer & Earn](../refer) — Access your referral link and share it with your network.\n- [Pricing & Subscriptions](../pricing) — Details on the Pro membership plans generating commissions.\n",
  "dashboard": "# Dashboard Overview\n\nThe Dashboard Overview is your central command center for real-time account safety monitoring, Instagram API rate limits, interaction metrics, and automated sales conversion funnels.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Dashboard](/dashboard)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Dashboard Overview](./images/dashboard-overview.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Dashboard overview showing KPI summary cards, rate limit health indicators, live activity stream, and conversion funnel.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Dashboard provides creators and businesses with instant visibility into how their Instagram automation is operating. It tracks outbound direct messages, revenue generated from automated customer checkouts, active reply flows, and account safety health in real time.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Monitor overall business performance through 30-day KPI cards.\n- Track Instagram API rate limits to prevent account throttling or bans.\n- Inspect real-time live activity feeds of automated customer conversations and replies.\n- Analyze sales conversion progression across Impression, Engagement, DM Started, and Conversion stages.\n- Review engagement summary metrics including response speed and DM open rate.\n- Manually refresh live telemetry data at any moment.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Check Account Safety Status\nAt the top of the dashboard, review the **Instagram Account Safety & Health** panel. Ensure the badge indicates `Account Safe`. Check your hourly DM quota bar and daily publish post limits before launching major marketing campaigns.\n\n### Step 2: Track Business KPIs\nReview the top metric strip for:\n- **Active Automations**: Total running rules and flows.\n- **Messages Sent (30d)**: Total direct messages dispatched to customers.\n- **Total Revenue (30d)**: Value of completed customer purchases originating from DMs and storefront.\n- **New Customers Reached**: Total unique leads engaged.\n\n### Step 3: Monitor Live Customer Interactions\nScroll through the **Activity Feed** to view inbound queries, keyword triggers, and bot responses with timestamps and agent tags. Use the pagination controls at the bottom of the feed to inspect older activity history.\n\n### Step 4: Evaluate the Conversion Funnel\nCheck the right-side **Conversion Funnel** to see drop-off rates between impressions, chat interactions, DM conversations, and final checkouts.\n\n## Available Options & Metrics\n\n| Metric / Control | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Refresh Button** | Instantly re-fetches latest telemetry, rate limits, and analytics from the server. |\n| **Hourly DM Quota** | Live progress bar of hourly DMs sent vs. Instagram API limit (default 200/hr) with remaining count. |\n| **Meta API Capacity** | Percentage of API capacity utilized with countdown timer to the next reset window. |\n| **24h Post Slots** | Daily publishing quota used and remaining slots available for posts and reels. |\n| **Health Status Badge** | Color-coded status (`SAFE`, `MODERATE`, `WARNING`, or `THROTTLED`). |\n| **Activity Pagination** | Navigate through pages of customer interactions and automated reply logs. |\n| **Avg Response Speed** | Average response latency for automated DM and comment replies. |\n| **DM Open Rate** | Percentage of dispatched direct messages opened and read by customers. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Automations Catalog](../automations/catalog) — Manage the automation rules that generate dashboard activity.\n- [Instagram Post Scheduler](../schedule) — Schedule posts and reels within your daily limits.\n- [Unified DM Inbox](../inbox/chat) — Jump into live customer conversations triggered on the dashboard.\n",
  "inbox/broadcast": "# Broadcast Direct Messages\n\nBroadcast Direct Messages enables creators and businesses to dispatch marketing announcements, flash sale alerts, and VIP invitations to segmented customer audiences.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Broadcast](/dashboard/inbox/broadcast)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Broadcast Direct Messages](./images/inbox-broadcast.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Broadcast DM dashboard showing campaign history cards, audience segment tags, scheduled dispatch dates, and campaign creation button.\n\n## Overview\n\nBroadcast DM allows you to re-engage warm leads and existing customers on Instagram at scale. By filtering your contacts into targeted segments, you can broadcast promotional offers, new product launches, or event invites while respecting Instagram API rate limits.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Create and schedule broadcast DM campaigns.\n- Target specific audience segments (e.g., VIP Buyers, High Engagement Leads, Active 24h Window Contacts).\n- View campaign dispatch status (`Scheduled`, `Processing`, `Sent`, `Completed`).\n- Monitor delivery counts and audience reach metrics per campaign.\n- Schedule campaigns for future delivery dates and times.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open Broadcast Dashboard\nNavigate to **Inbox > Broadcast** from the sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Create a Broadcast Campaign\n1. Click the **Create Broadcast** button in the top right.\n2. Enter a descriptive **Campaign Title** (e.g., *\"Summer Launch VIP Invitation\"*).\n3. Select your target **Audience Segment** or choose selected contacts from your Contacts CRM.\n4. Compose your direct message text with personalized customer tags.\n5. Attach an optional product card or link button.\n\n### Step 3: Schedule or Send\n- Select **Send Immediately** or set a scheduled date and time.\n- Review campaign details and confirm. AnyDM automatically queues and delivers messages with safe jitter spacing to protect your account health.\n\n> **Video tutorial placeholder**\n>\n> Add a video demonstrating how to create an Instagram DM broadcast campaign to previous buyers for a flash sale.\n\n## Available Broadcast Fields & Campaign Data\n\n| Field | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Campaign Title** | Internal reference name for the broadcast. |\n| **Audience Segment** | Targeted group (e.g., All Leads, VIP Segment, 24h Active Contacts). |\n| **Schedule Date** | Timestamp when message delivery is initiated. |\n| **Campaign Status** | `Scheduled` (Awaiting trigger) or `Sent` / `Completed` (Delivered). |\n| **Message Content** | Personalized DM text and media payload delivered to recipients. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Contacts CRM](./contacts) — Select and filter contacts to build custom broadcast segments.\n- [Unified DM Live Chat](./chat) — Handle customer replies generated by your broadcast campaigns.\n- [Dashboard Overview](../dashboard) — Monitor hourly DM limits during active broadcasts.\n",
  "inbox/chat": "# Unified DM Live Chat\n\nThe Unified DM Live Chat is a fast, multi-threaded communication workspace for chatting with Instagram followers, managing customer support conversations, and taking over bot interactions.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Inbox](/dashboard/inbox)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Unified DM Live Chat](./images/inbox-chat.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Unified Chat interface displaying active conversation threads list, chat window with message bubbles, media attachment players, AI response suggestions, and customer detail sidebar.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe AnyDM Inbox aggregates all your Instagram Direct Messages into a synchronized desktop workspace. You can seamlessly switch between automated AI responses and human agent interventions, send product cards and photos, view customer order histories, and resolve customer queries quickly.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Manage multiple concurrent Instagram direct message conversations in real time.\n- Search chat conversations by customer name, username handle, or message keywords.\n- Send rich text, emojis, quick replies, product checkout cards, and media attachments (photos and playable videos).\n- Toggle bot automation on or off for individual customer threads (*Human Takeover Mode*).\n- Inspect customer profile details, follow status, total interactions, and lead score in the side panel.\n- Filter conversations by tags, unread status, or lead stage.\n- Delete or archive obsolete message threads.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Select a Conversation Thread\n1. Navigate to **Inbox** from the main sidebar.\n2. In the left-hand thread list, click on any customer conversation to load their chat history.\n3. Unread messages and new inbound inquiries are highlighted at the top of the queue.\n\n### Step 2: Send Messages & Product Cards\n1. Type your response in the message input at the bottom of the chat window.\n2. Click the **Product / Shopping Bag** icon to quickly attach a product checkout card.\n3. Click the **Media** icon to upload and send images or video attachments.\n4. Press Enter or click **Send** to dispatch the message directly into the customer's Instagram DM inbox.\n\n### Step 3: Enable Human Takeover\n- When a complex query requires manual support, click the **Pause Bot / Takeover** button at the top of the chat.\n- While paused, automated bots will not trigger on this user's messages, allowing you to converse naturally.\n- Click **Resume Bot** when finished to re-enable automated flows.\n\n## Available Chat Controls & Indicators\n\n| Control / Indicator | Function |\n|---|---|\n| **Thread List** | List of all Instagram direct message conversations with live snippet previews. |\n| **Search Filter** | Find specific customer chats by name, handle, or recent message content. |\n| **Bot Status Toggle** | Switch between automated bot handling and manual agent takeover. |\n| **Product Card Inserter** | Instantly embed a catalog product card with a clickable checkout CTA into the chat. |\n| **Media Player** | In-app player for previewing video and voice note attachments sent or received. |\n| **Customer Info Sidebar** | Shows follower status, lead score, previous orders, and 24-hour window countdown. |\n| **Refresh Stream** | Manually synchronizes conversation updates with Instagram servers. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Contacts CRM](./contacts) — Manage customer profiles, tags, and engagement scores.\n- [Broadcast Campaigns](./broadcast) — Send announcements to segmented groups of contacts.\n- [Product Catalog](../products/catalog) — Items available to insert into direct messages.\n",
  "inbox/contacts": "# Contacts CRM & Lead Intelligence\n\nContacts CRM is your customer database for tracking Instagram leads, monitoring interaction frequency, assessing lead scores, and tracking the official 24-hour messaging window.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Contacts CRM](/dashboard/inbox/contacts)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Contacts CRM Table](./images/inbox-contacts.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Contacts CRM table showing user avatars, Instagram handles, interaction counters, lead scores, 24h/23h messaging window countdown badges, and multi-contact broadcast selector.\n\n## Overview\n\nEvery customer who interacts with your Instagram posts, reels, or direct messages is captured in your AnyDM CRM. The Contacts directory provides actionable intelligence on your most engaged followers, tracks their customer journey, and displays live countdowns for Instagram's official 24-hour customer service messaging window.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Browse, search, and paginate through your entire contact list.\n- View customer Instagram avatars, full names, usernames, and profile details.\n- Track total interactions, product inquiries, and automated lead scores.\n- Filter contacts by messaging window status: `All`, `Within 24h`, `Within 23h`, or `Expired Window`.\n- Sort contacts by most recent interaction, highest lead score, or interaction volume.\n- Multi-select contacts with checkboxes to quickly launch targeted broadcast campaigns.\n- Open direct one-on-one chats with any contact in the Unified DM Inbox with a single click.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Browse & Search Contacts\n1. Open **Inbox > Contacts** from the sidebar.\n2. Use the **Search Bar** to look up contacts by username, full name, or last message content.\n3. Review key columns: **Interactions**, **Lead Score**, and **Follow Status**.\n\n### Step 2: Filter by 24-Hour Messaging Window\n1. Use the window filter tabs above the table:\n   - **24h Active**: Users who sent an inbound message in the last 24 hours (standard API messaging allowed).\n   - **23h Warning**: Contacts approaching window expiry (1 hour remaining).\n   - **Expired**: Contacts outside the active window.\n\n### Step 3: Select Contacts for Broadcast\n1. Click the checkboxes on specific contact rows or click the header checkbox to select all contacts on the page.\n2. Click **Broadcast to Selected** to create a bulk DM campaign specifically targeted to these users.\n\n### Step 4: Jump into Direct Chat\nClick on any contact's name or the **Chat** icon on their row to immediately open their live thread in the Unified Inbox.\n\n## Available Columns & Lead Attributes\n\n| Attribute | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Contact / Handle** | Instagram avatar, username (`@handle`), and full profile name. |\n| **Interactions** | Cumulative count of comments, DMs, and story mentions received from this user. |\n| **Enquiries** | Total product or pricing inquiries initiated by the user. |\n| **Lead Score** | Algorithmic score reflecting user purchase intent and activity level. |\n| **Last Inbound Time** | Timestamp and snippet of the customer's most recent message. |\n| **24h Window Timer** | Live countdown timer indicating remaining time in the Meta 24-hour standard reply window. |\n| **Following Status** | Shows whether the contact follows your business and whether your account follows them. |\n| **Multi-Select Checkbox** | Used to pick recipients for bulk broadcast dispatches. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Unified DM Live Chat](./chat) — Direct conversation interface with selected contacts.\n- [Broadcast Direct Messages](./broadcast) — Dispatch mass messages to selected contact cohorts.\n- [Orders Management](../products/orders) — View order history for buyers in your CRM.\n",
  "pricing": "# Pricing & Subscriptions\n\nExplore AnyDM membership tiers, upgrade to Creator Pro for unlimited DM automations and AI tokens, and manage your billing cycle.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Pricing](/dashboard/pricing)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Pricing Plans Matrix](./images/pricing-overview.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Pricing page displaying the Free Trial and Creator Pro tier cards, feature comparison checklist, active subscription expiry status, and Razorpay checkout action.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM offers a transparent freemium model. New creators begin with a full-featured Free Trial to experience automated direct messages and storefront capabilities. Upgrading to **Creator Pro** unlocks unlimited high-speed DM triggers, master AI model access, unlimited product listings, and priority webhook processing.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Compare feature availability between the **Free Trial** and **Creator Pro** plans.\n- Check current subscription status, active plan tier, and trial days remaining.\n- Upgrade or renew your Creator Pro subscription seamlessly via Razorpay (UPI, Credit/Debit Cards, Net Banking).\n- Redeem earned reward points for free 30-day Pro plan extensions.\n- View upcoming billing dates and payment receipts.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Review Plan Comparison\n1. Open **Pricing** from the main sidebar.\n2. Review the plan comparison matrix to select the tier that matches your business needs.\n\n### Step 2: Upgrade to Creator Pro\n1. Click the **Upgrade to Pro (₹499/mo)** button on the Pro plan card.\n2. The secure **Razorpay Checkout** popup will appear.\n3. Select your preferred payment method (UPI, Google Pay, PhonePe, Cards, or Netbanking).\n4. Complete payment. Your account is upgraded instantly, and all Pro features activate immediately.\n\n### Step 3: Extend Subscription Using Points\n- If you have accumulated **100+ Reward Points** through referrals, click **Extend with 100 Points** to add 30 free days of Pro access to your account.\n\n## Plan Comparison Matrix\n\n| Feature / Capability | Free Trial | Creator Pro (₹499 / month) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Direct Message Automation** | Standard Limit | **Unlimited Fast Triggers** |\n| **Instagram Post Scheduler** | Basic Post Queue | **Unlimited Scheduling & Reels** |\n| **AI Smart Autopilot** | Custom API Key Required | **Included (Master AI Token)** |\n| **Product Catalog Listings** | Up to 3 Products | **Unlimited Products & Orders** |\n| **Link-in-Bio Customization** | Standard Themes | **All Premium Glass Themes** |\n| **Broadcast Direct Messages** | Basic | **Advanced Segment Filtering** |\n| **Customer Support** | Community | **Priority Direct Support** |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Refer & Earn](../refer) — Earn free months of Creator Pro by inviting fellow creators.\n- [Connected Accounts](../settings/accounts) — Manage connected Instagram profiles under your subscription.\n- [Creator Hub](../creator) — Earn affiliate commissions when users upgrade via your link.\n",
  "products/catalog": "# Product Catalog\n\nThe Product Catalog is where you manage your digital products, e-books, courses, services, physical goods, and consultation offerings sold through Instagram DMs and your store.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Product Catalog](/dashboard/products/catalog)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Product Catalog](./images/products-catalog.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Product Catalog dashboard showing product cards, pricing, stock levels, category filters, search bar, and Instagram import modal trigger.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM turns your Instagram profile into a social commerce store. The Product Catalog houses all your sellable items, complete with checkout links, automated direct message triggers, pricing tiers, and delivery files.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Browse, search, and filter all products in your inventory.\n- Import products and media directly from your Instagram posts and reels.\n- Add new digital downloads, services, courses, or physical items.\n- Edit product details, pricing, discount rates, inventory, and delivery assets.\n- Toggle product availability (Active / Inactive) or delete products.\n- Quick-copy public product purchase links to share in chat or social bios.\n- Track total orders and sales generated by each product.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Access the Catalog\nNavigate to **Products > All Products** from the sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Search and Filter Items\n- Use the **Search Bar** to find products by title or description.\n- Use the **Filter Tabs** (`All`, `Digital`, `Physical`, `Course`, `Service`) to narrow down items.\n\n### Step 3: Manage Products\n- Click the **Pencil / Edit** icon on any product card to modify pricing, description, or files.\n- Click the **Trash** icon to delete a product.\n- Click **Copy Link** to paste the checkout URL into DMs or social posts.\n\n### Step 4: Import from Instagram\nClick **Import from Instagram** to pull media and captions from your published Instagram posts and convert them into store products automatically.\n\n## Product Types & Catalog Attributes\n\n| Attribute / Action | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Product Type** | Digital Download (PDF/ZIP), Physical Good, Video Course, or 1-on-1 Consultation Service. |\n| **Price & Currency** | Regular selling price and optional discounted comparison price. |\n| **Stock / Inventory** | Inventory count tracking or unlimited digital delivery mode. |\n| **Active Status** | Toggle whether the product is currently purchasable by customers. |\n| **Direct Checkout Link** | Public link leading directly to the AnyDM seamless checkout screen. |\n| **Orders Counter** | Total completed purchases recorded for this item. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Create Product](./create) — Step-by-step guide for creating and configuring new products.\n- [Orders Management](./orders) — View customer orders, payment status, and customer details.\n- [Product Auto-Replies](./replies) — Link specific product cards to automated Instagram DM responses.\n- [Creator Storefront](./website) — Customize the public website where all catalog products appear.\n",
  "products/create": "# Create & Edit Product\n\nConfigure product details, pricing models, downloadable digital files, media galleries, inventory, and automated delivery fulfillment for your items.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Create New Product](/dashboard/products/catalog/create)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Product Creation Form](./images/products-create.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Product Creation editor with product title, description editor, pricing inputs, media uploader, digital file attachment zone, and preview card.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Product Creation screen gives you all the tools required to publish sellable goods. When a customer purchases a product through AnyDM checkout, the system processes payment via Razorpay, automatically delivers download links or access instructions, and records customer order details.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Choose product format: **Digital Download**, **Course / Content**, **Service / Consultation**, or **Physical Product**.\n- Set base price, original comparison price (strikethrough discount), and currency.\n- Upload product cover images and multi-image media galleries.\n- Upload digital delivery files (PDFs, ZIPs, ebooks, design presets, video links).\n- Write rich descriptions with markdown formatting and bullet points.\n- Set inventory counts or enable unlimited stock.\n- Configure automated order confirmation messages and download instructions.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Set Basic Information\n1. Open **Products > All Products** and click **+ Add Product**.\n2. Enter the **Product Name** (e.g., *\"Ultimate Creator Guide 2026\"*).\n3. Select the **Category / Product Type**.\n4. Write a detailed **Description** highlighting what buyers receive.\n\n### Step 2: Set Pricing & Inventory\n1. Enter the **Selling Price** (e.g., `₹499`).\n2. Optional: Enter an **Original Price** (e.g., `₹999`) to show a discount badge.\n3. For digital goods, select **Unlimited Inventory**. For physical items, enter available stock units.\n\n### Step 3: Upload Product Media & Delivery Files\n1. Click **Upload Product Images** to add showcase photos.\n2. Under **Fulfillment / Download File**, upload the PDF, ZIP archive, or asset file delivered upon successful payment.\n3. If selling a consultation service or course, provide the meeting/course access link and instructions.\n\n### Step 4: Save & Publish\n1. Review the generated product summary card.\n2. Click **Publish Product**. Your product is now live on your bio page and ready for automated DM sales.\n\n> **Video tutorial placeholder**\n>\n> Add a video demonstrating how to create a digital product, upload downloadable assets, and sell it via Instagram DM triggers.\n\n## Available Product Configuration Fields\n\n| Field | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| **Product Title** | Customer-facing name of the item. |\n| **Product Type** | `Digital`, `Course`, `Service`, or `Physical`. Determines delivery workflow. |\n| **Price (₹)** | The checkout purchase price charged to the buyer. |\n| **Original Price (₹)** | Optional higher strikethrough price for promotional discounts. |\n| **Product Description** | Full sales copy and features list. |\n| **Media Images** | High-resolution thumbnail and gallery images. |\n| **Digital Download File** | Asset securely hosted and delivered to buyers after verified payment. |\n| **Access URL / Instructions** | Meeting link or external access instructions for services and courses. |\n| **Inventory Count** | Stock units available for sale. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Product Catalog](./catalog) — Manage all published products.\n- [Orders Management](./orders) — Track purchases and customer downloads.\n- [Product Auto-Replies](./replies) — Automatically send this product's checkout link when followers comment.\n",
  "products/orders": "# Orders & Fulfillment\n\nManage customer purchases, track payment statuses, monitor sales earnings, inspect order details, and oversee fulfillment.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Orders](/dashboard/products/orders)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Orders Management Dashboard](./images/products-orders.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Orders dashboard showing sales metrics cards (Today's Sales, Pending Orders, Completed Orders, Pending Settlement), searchable order list, payment status chips, and order detail drawer.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Orders dashboard provides comprehensive transactional management for your AnyDM digital store. Whenever a customer completes checkout via direct messages, bio links, or your creator website, the order is logged here with customer contact details, items purchased, transaction IDs, and settlement status.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- View financial summaries: Today's Sales, Total Earnings, Completed Orders, and Pending Payout Settlement.\n- Search orders by Customer Name, Email, Order ID, or Product Title.\n- Filter orders by status (`All`, `Pending`, `Completed`, `Cancelled`, `Refunded`).\n- Inspect individual order details (buyer phone number, shipping address for physical goods, delivery status, and payment method).\n- Update fulfillment status (Mark as Shipped / Completed).\n- Copy tracking URLs and customer info for communication.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Review Sales Metrics\nAt the top of the Orders page, check your store performance metrics:\n- **Today's Sales**: Gross revenue collected today.\n- **Pending Orders**: Orders awaiting review or physical dispatch.\n- **Completed Orders**: Successfully processed and delivered transactions.\n- **Pending Settlement**: Earnings queued for transfer to your verified bank account.\n\n### Step 2: Search and Inspect Orders\n1. Enter customer name, email, or order number into the search bar.\n2. Click on any order row in the table to open the **Order Details Modal**.\n3. Review purchased items, unit price, quantity, buyer details, and payment confirmation.\n\n### Step 3: Manage Fulfillment\n- For digital goods: Delivery is instant and automated. The system records file download access.\n- For physical goods: Review shipping address, pack items, and update status to `Shipped` or `Delivered`.\n\n## Available Order Fields & Statuses\n\n| Field / Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Order ID** | Unique transaction identifier (e.g., `#ORD-9281`). |\n| **Customer Info** | Buyer name, email address, phone number, and Instagram handle if available. |\n| **Product & Qty** | Purchased item title, variant, and quantity ordered. |\n| **Total Amount** | Gross order payment amount including any applicable taxes and fees. |\n| **Payment Status** | `PAID` (Payment captured), `PENDING` (Checkout initiated), `FAILED`, or `REFUNDED`. |\n| **Fulfillment Status** | `COMPLETED` (Files delivered / fulfilled) or `PROCESSING`. |\n| **Date & Time** | Timestamp of transaction creation. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Product Catalog](./catalog) — Review stock and active store items.\n- [Seller KYC Settings](../settings/kyc) — Verify your bank details to receive order payout settlements.\n- [Creator Hub](../creator) — Track affiliate revenue and payout requests.\n",
  "products/replies": "# Product Auto-Replies\n\nConfigure automated Instagram Direct Message replies and public comment responses linked directly to your catalog products.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Product Replies](/dashboard/products/replies)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Product Auto-Replies](./images/products-replies.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Product Auto-Replies management page showing product response cards, mapped keywords, custom DM text templates, and public comment reply variations.\n\n## Overview\n\nProduct Auto-Replies connect your product catalog with AnyDM's Instagram automation engine. When users express interest in a specific product by commenting on your reels or messaging your inbox, these tailored templates automatically dispatch the product's image, description, and direct purchase link.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Map specific products to automated comment trigger keywords (e.g., product name or code).\n- Customize the direct message card format sent to interested buyers.\n- Define multiple randomized public comment reply variations to maintain natural engagement.\n- Include direct checkout buttons, discount codes, and product links.\n- Toggle auto-replies on or off per product.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Select a Product\n1. Navigate to **Products > Quick Replies**.\n2. Select the catalog product you want to configure automation for.\n\n### Step 2: Define Trigger Keywords\n1. Enter the trigger keywords associated with this product (e.g., `DRESS, BUY, DETAILS, STORE`).\n2. Set matching sensitivity to trigger whenever these words appear in comments on your posts.\n\n### Step 3: Customize Message Templates\n1. Edit the **DM Response Text**: Include greeting, product highlights, and a call-to-action.\n2. Ensure the **Product Checkout Link** button is enabled.\n3. Add 3–5 **Public Comment Reply Variations** (e.g., *\"Just sent the details to your DMs! 👗\"*, *\"Check your inbox for the link! ✨\"*).\n\n### Step 4: Activate Auto-Replies\nToggle the rule status to **Active** and click **Save Changes**.\n\n## Available Reply Settings\n\n| Setting / Field | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Associated Product** | The specific catalog item linked to this auto-response flow. |\n| **Trigger Keywords** | Keywords that activate this reply when detected in comments or DMs. |\n| **DM Template** | Customizable direct message sent privately to the user. |\n| **Checkout Button Text** | CTA button text (e.g., *\"Buy Now - ₹499\"* or *\"View Product\"*). |\n| **Comment Variations** | List of public comment replies rotated randomly to avoid repetitive spam detection. |\n| **Rule Status** | Master toggle to enable or pause automated replies for this product. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Product Catalog](./catalog) — Manage the items linked to your reply rules.\n- [Visual Flow Builder](../automations/builder) — Design multi-step interactive conversation trees.\n- [Unified DM Inbox](../inbox/chat) — View and take over automated customer conversations.\n",
  "products/website": "# Creator Storefront Website\n\nConfigure and personalize your standalone e-commerce storefront website powered by AnyDM.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Creator Website](/dashboard/products/website)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Creator Storefront Settings](./images/products-website.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Creator Storefront customization page showing domain options, brand logo uploader, hero banner customizer, featured products selector, and live store preview.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM automatically generates a dedicated creator storefront website where your complete product catalog is hosted. Customers can browse all your digital goods, courses, physical products, and services in a responsive e-commerce environment.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Customize your store's public brand name, logo, and announcement banner.\n- Configure custom store domain or use your standard AnyDM creator URL (`username.anydm.in`).\n- Feature specific hero products at the top of your shop.\n- Organize products into browsable store collections and categories.\n- Customize store policies: Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, and Refund Policy.\n- Preview your live creator storefront on mobile and desktop views.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open Storefront Settings\nNavigate to **Products > Website** from the sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Configure Store Branding\n1. Enter your **Store Name** and tagline.\n2. Upload your high-resolution **Store Logo** and **Hero Banner**.\n3. Set an **Announcement Banner** message (e.g., *\"Free shipping on orders above ₹999!\"* or *\"Use code LAUNCH20 for 20% off!\"*).\n\n### Step 3: Curate Featured Products\n1. Select which catalog items appear in the **Featured Collection** on your homepage.\n2. Arrange product display order.\n\n### Step 4: Review and Publish\n1. Review the storefront preview on the right.\n2. Click **Save & Update Store**.\n3. Click **Visit Storefront** to open your live shop in a new tab.\n\n## Available Storefront Settings\n\n| Setting | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| **Store Name** | Main branding title shown in header, SEO titles, and receipts. |\n| **Store Logo & Favicon** | Visual identity displayed across your storefront. |\n| **Hero Banner** | Prominent graphic introducing your brand on the store homepage. |\n| **Announcement Bar** | Top banner for sitewide alerts, discount codes, or news. |\n| **Featured Products** | Hand-picked products prioritized on your storefront home page. |\n| **Custom Domain** | Connect your own custom domain (e.g., `shop.yourbrand.com`). |\n| **Legal Pages** | Editable Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, and Refund guidelines. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Product Catalog](./catalog) — Add and manage products appearing on your storefront.\n- [Orders Management](./orders) — Track purchases originating from your storefront.\n- [Link-in-Bio Overview](../bio) — Add direct link to your store on your bio page.\n",
  "refer": "# Refer & Earn\n\nEarn reward points by inviting creators and friends to AnyDM, unlock free monthly extensions of Creator Pro, and track your referral network.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Refer & Earn](/dashboard/refer)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Refer & Earn Program](./images/refer-overview.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Refer & Earn dashboard showing unique referral code, copy link button, points earned summary, redeem free pro button, milestone tier badges, and referral history table.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe AnyDM Referral Program rewards you for sharing the platform with other creators. Every successful referral earns reward points that can be redeemed for free months of the Creator Pro plan or converted into milestone badges.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- View and customize your personal unique **Referral Code** and invite link (`/signup?ref=CODE`).\n- Copy and share your referral link across social media, groups, and direct messages.\n- Track real-time referral metrics: Total Points Earned, Successful Signups, and Pro Days Claimed.\n- Redeem 100 Reward Points for 1 Month of Free Creator Pro access.\n- Complete bonus social engagement tasks (e.g., Follow AnyDM on Instagram) to earn instant bonus points.\n- Inspect the referral history log showing referred users, signup dates, and point allocation status.\n- Enter a friend's referral code if you signed up without one.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Share Your Referral Link\n1. Navigate to **Refer & Earn** from the sidebar.\n2. Click **Copy Link** to copy your personalized invitation URL.\n3. Share your link with creators, influencers, and digital businesses.\n\n### Step 2: Customize Your Referral Code\n1. Click the **Pencil / Edit** icon next to your referral code.\n2. Enter your custom vanity code (e.g., `ALEX2026`).\n3. Click **Save** to update your code and link.\n\n### Step 3: Redeem Points for Free Pro\n1. When your balance reaches **100 points**, the **Redeem 1 Month Pro** button becomes active.\n2. Click **Redeem Now** to instantly extend your Pro membership subscription by 30 days without charging your card.\n\n### Step 4: Claim Social Bonus Points\n- Click the **Follow on Instagram (+10 pts)** task card.\n- Follow `@anydm.in` and click **Verify & Claim** to receive your bonus points.\n\n## Reward Points Economy & Milestones\n\n| Action / Tier | Reward Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Invite New User** | +50 Reward Points per successful user signup. |\n| **Instagram Social Task** | +10 Reward Points (one-time bonus upon verification). |\n| **1 Month Pro Extension** | Costs 100 Reward Points (Extends subscription by 30 days). |\n| **Bronze Tier** | 1–3 Successful Referrals. |\n| **Silver Tier** | 4–9 Successful Referrals. |\n| **Gold Ambassador Tier** | 10+ Successful Referrals with priority support perks. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Pricing & Plans](../pricing) — View full Pro features unlocked through point redemptions.\n- [Creator Hub](../creator) — Monetize your audience with cash commissions as an approved VIP Creator.\n",
  "schedule": "# Schedule Posts & Publisher\n\nThe Instagram Post Scheduler allows you to plan, create, preview, schedule, and automatically publish Instagram Reels, Images, Videos, Stories, and Carousels.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Post Scheduler](/dashboard/schedule)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Instagram Post Scheduler](./images/schedule-overview.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Post Scheduler page showing scheduled and published posts in grid/list view, filtering tabs, upload modal, and mobile feed preview mockup.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM Scheduler connects directly to the official Meta Graph API to publish your content automatically without requiring push notifications or manual approvals. You can prepare content in advance, write engaging captions with AI assistance, configure custom reel cover thumbnails, and monitor publishing status in real time.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Schedule multiple post formats: **Reels**, **Single Images**, **Videos**, **Stories**, and **Multi-Image Carousels**.\n- Upload media directly with Cloudinary-backed high-speed cloud processing.\n- Select or upload custom video cover thumbnails for Instagram Reels.\n- Write captions with built-in emoji picker, hashtag tools, and AI caption generation.\n- Choose **Publish Now** for immediate delivery or set a future publication date and time.\n- Filter scheduled posts by status (`ALL`, `SCHEDULED`, `PUBLISHED`, `FAILED`, `DRAFT`) and media type.\n- Preview posts in realistic Instagram Mobile and Desktop feed simulators before publishing.\n- Edit, cancel, or reschedule pending posts.\n- Inspect direct Instagram permalinks for published posts or view detailed error logs for failed attempts.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Create a New Post\n1. Navigate to **Schedule Posts** from the sidebar.\n2. Click **+ Schedule New Post**.\n3. Select the content format: `REELS`, `IMAGE`, `VIDEO`, `STORIES`, or `CAROUSEL`.\n\n### Step 2: Upload Media & Configure Thumbnail\n1. Drag and drop your image or video files, or click to upload.\n2. For Reels and Videos, select a specific video frame or upload a custom cover thumbnail image.\n3. Toggle **Share to Feed** if you want your Reel visible on both your profile grid and the Reels tab.\n\n### Step 3: Write Caption & Hashtags\n1. Enter your post caption in the editor.\n2. Use the **Emoji Picker** or click **AI Caption Assistant** to generate engaging, viral captions.\n3. Add relevant hashtags to maximize reach.\n\n### Step 4: Schedule or Publish\n1. To post immediately, click **Publish Now**.\n2. To schedule for later, choose your target **Date and Time**, then click **Schedule Post**.\n3. Monitor your post status on the calendar and feed list.\n\n> **Video tutorial placeholder**\n>\n> Add a video tutorial demonstrating how to schedule a batch of Instagram Reels with custom thumbnails and AI captions.\n\n## Available Options & Post Types\n\n| Option / Field | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Reels (`REELS`)** | Full-screen vertical video posts published to your Instagram Reels feed and profile. |\n| **Carousel (`CAROUSEL`)** | Multi-slide posts supporting multiple uploaded images in a swipeable sequence. |\n| **Images & Video (`IMAGE` / `VIDEO`)** | Standard feed photo and video posts. |\n| **Stories (`STORIES`)** | 24-hour ephemeral story posts. |\n| **Custom Cover Thumbnail** | Select an exact video timestamp or upload an image as your reel cover. |\n| **Share to Feed Toggle** | Controls whether a published Reel is also placed on your main profile feed grid. |\n| **Publishing Status** | Live status indicators: `DRAFT`, `SCHEDULED`, `PROCESSING`, `PUBLISHED`, `FAILED`, `CANCELLED`. |\n| **Instagram Permalink** | Direct link to open and view the live published post on Instagram. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Automations Catalog](../automations/catalog) — Attach comment-to-DM triggers to your scheduled reels.\n- [Dashboard Overview](../dashboard) — Monitor daily publishing limits (Meta 24-hour post quotas).\n- [Connected Accounts](../settings/accounts) — Manage connected Instagram business accounts.\n",
  "settings/accounts": "# Connected Accounts & Security\n\nManage your connected Instagram Business accounts, link Google or Email authentication credentials, and configure account security settings.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Connected Accounts](/dashboard/settings/accounts)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Connected Accounts Dashboard](./images/settings-accounts.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Connected Accounts page showing connected Instagram profiles, Facebook Page bindings, Google SSO linking status, and account security controls.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM connects directly to Instagram and Facebook via the official Meta Graph API. In the Connected Accounts settings, you can link multiple Instagram Business or Creator accounts, switch active accounts, renew expiring access tokens, and link authentication providers for seamless login.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Connect and disconnect Instagram Professional (Business or Creator) accounts.\n- View connected Instagram handle, follower count, profile avatar, and Facebook Page name.\n- Switch the active Instagram account for your current AnyDM session.\n- Re-authenticate or refresh Meta access tokens to ensure uninterrupted webhooks.\n- Link or unlink Google SSO and Email/Password credentials for flexible login.\n- Review account security details and active sessions.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Connect an Instagram Account\n1. Navigate to **Settings > Manage Accounts**.\n2. Click **+ Connect Instagram Account**.\n3. You will be redirected to the secure Meta OAuth authorization dialog.\n4. Select the Facebook Page and Instagram Professional Account you wish to manage with AnyDM.\n5. Grant required permissions (Messaging, Comments, Insights) and confirm.\n6. Once redirected back, your connected Instagram profile will appear in your account list.\n\n### Step 2: Switch Active Account\n- If managing multiple creator profiles, click **Switch Active** on the account card you wish to manage. The entire dashboard, inbox, and automation flows will update to reflect that account.\n\n### Step 3: Link Login Providers\n- Under **Authentication Providers**, click **Link with Google** to enable single-click Google Sign-In on your existing AnyDM workspace.\n\n## Available Account Options & Statuses\n\n| Option / Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Active Instagram Account** | The currently selected profile receiving webhooks and sending automated replies. |\n| **Meta Token Health** | Real-time status of your API authorization token (`Valid`, `Expiring Soon`, or `Needs Reconnection`). |\n| **Facebook Page Binding** | The official Facebook Page linked to your Instagram professional account. |\n| **Google Authentication** | Status of connected Google SSO account for passwordless sign-in. |\n| **Disconnect Account** | Safely removes the Instagram account authorization from AnyDM. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Dashboard Overview](../../dashboard) — Check hourly rate limits and API health for your active account.\n- [Automations Catalog](../../automations/catalog) — Manage automation flows running on your active account.\n- [Workspace Settings](./workspace) — Configure workspace profile and team attributes.\n",
  "settings/ai": "# AI Agent Configuration\n\nConfigure your AI assistant persona, system instructions, business knowledge base, support guidelines, and API token keys.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open AI Settings](/dashboard/settings/ai)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: AI Settings Configuration](./images/settings-ai.png)\n> **Screenshot:** AI Agent Configuration dashboard showing Persona Prompt editor, business knowledge base cards (Store Hours, Return Policy, Address, Phone), and master AI token status.\n\n## Overview\n\nAnyDM features an intelligent conversational AI agent capable of answering customer questions in direct messages, recommending products, and sharing store policies 24/7. In AI Settings, you can train your AI on your specific business details and define its conversational tone.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Customize your AI Assistant's **Persona & System Prompt** (e.g., tone of voice, emoji usage, brand voice).\n- Configure business knowledge details: **Store Address**, **Business Hours**, **Customer Support Phone**, and **Shipping/Return Policies**.\n- Enable or disable automated AI responses in Instagram Direct Messages.\n- Creator Pro accounts automatically use the AnyDM Master AI Token without requiring custom OpenAI/Gemini API keys.\n- Add custom API keys for third-party LLM providers if preferred.\n- Test prompt responses with sample customer questions.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open AI Settings\nNavigate to **Settings > AI Settings** from the sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Define Agent Persona\n1. In the **System Instructions** text box, define how the AI should represent your brand (e.g., *\"You are the friendly AI assistant for Alex Rivera Studio. Keep responses concise, warm, and helpful. Always encourage customers to check our digital catalog\"*).\n2. Set response length preferences and tone parameters.\n\n### Step 3: Populate Business Knowledge\n1. Under **Business Information**, enter:\n   - **Store Location / Address**: Physical studio or online store base.\n   - **Operating Hours**: (e.g., *\"Mon–Fri 9 AM – 6 PM IST\"*).\n   - **Contact Phone / Email**: Official support email or WhatsApp contact.\n   - **Return & Refund Policy**: Explicit terms on digital downloads or physical goods.\n2. The AI uses this data to answer incoming customer questions accurately.\n\n### Step 4: Save & Activate\nClick **Save AI Configuration**. Your AI agent is now active and will use this knowledge when generating direct message responses.\n\n## Available AI Settings & Knowledge Fields\n\n| Setting / Field | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| **System Prompt / Persona** | Core behavioral guidelines and tone instructing the AI how to converse. |\n| **Store Hours** | Business operating schedule shared with inquiring customers. |\n| **Location & Address** | Physical store or dispatch origin details. |\n| **Return & Refund Policy** | Policy rules used when customers ask about refunds or exchanges. |\n| **Support Phone & Email** | Escalation contact details for complex issues. |\n| **Master AI Token** | Built-in high-speed AI engine included with Creator Pro. |\n| **Custom API Key** | Optional custom OpenAI / Gemini API key configuration for Free Trial users. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Unified DM Live Chat](../inbox/chat) — Monitor AI responses and take over conversations when necessary.\n- [Automations Catalog](../automations/catalog) — Complement AI chat with rule-based keyword triggers.\n- [Product Catalog](../products/catalog) — Products referenced automatically by the AI during customer chats.\n",
  "settings/kyc": "# Seller KYC & Bank Verification\n\nComplete mandatory identity verification, submit your PAN and Aadhaar details, and connect your bank account to receive customer order payouts.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Seller KYC](/dashboard/settings/kyc)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Seller KYC Verification Form](./images/settings-kyc.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Seller KYC verification screen showing PAN card input, Aadhaar number input, Bank Account Details (Account Number, IFSC, Bank Name), and verification status badge.\n\n## Overview\n\nTo comply with Indian financial regulations and enable direct bank settlement payouts for products sold via AnyDM, creators must submit their Seller KYC (Know Your Customer) details. Once verified by our compliance team, sales revenue and affiliate earnings are transferred directly to your bank account.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Submit your legal Full Name matching your bank and tax documents.\n- Enter your Permanent Account Number (**PAN**).\n- Enter your **Aadhaar Number** for identity confirmation.\n- Enter your receiving **Bank Account Number**, Confirm Account Number, and **Bank IFSC Code**.\n- Track real-time verification status: `PENDING`, `SUBMITTED`, `APPROVED`, or `REJECTED`.\n- Receive bank settlement payouts for customer store purchases and creator commissions.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open KYC Form\nNavigate to **Settings > Seller KYC** from the sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Fill Identity Information\n1. Enter your **Legal Full Name** exactly as it appears on your bank account and PAN card.\n2. Enter your 10-character **PAN Number** (e.g., `ABCDE1234F`).\n3. Enter your 12-digit **Aadhaar Number**.\n\n### Step 3: Enter Bank Account Details\n1. Enter your **Bank Name** (e.g., *HDFC Bank, State Bank of India, ICICI*).\n2. Enter your **Bank Account Number**.\n3. Re-enter your account number in **Confirm Account Number**.\n4. Enter the 11-character **Bank IFSC Code** (e.g., `HDFC0001234`).\n\n### Step 4: Submit for Verification\n1. Review all entered details for precision.\n2. Click **Submit KYC for Verification**.\n3. Your application is submitted to the compliance queue. Approvals are typically completed within 24–48 business hours.\n\n## Available KYC Fields & Verification Statuses\n\n| Field / Status | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Legal Full Name** | Full name registered with tax authorities and bank records. |\n| **PAN Number** | 10-digit Permanent Account Number required for tax reporting. |\n| **Aadhaar Number** | 12-digit national identity number. |\n| **Bank Account Number** | Bank destination account for electronic fund transfers (NEFT/IMPS). |\n| **Bank IFSC** | Indian Financial System Code identifying your specific bank branch. |\n| **Status: PENDING** | KYC form has not yet been submitted. |\n| **Status: SUBMITTED** | Under active review by compliance administrators. |\n| **Status: APPROVED** | KYC approved. Automatic payout settlements are active. |\n| **Status: REJECTED** | Discrepancy detected. Review feedback notes and resubmit corrected info. |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Orders & Fulfillment](../products/orders) — View pending order earnings awaiting settlement.\n- [Creator Hub](../creator) — Payout withdrawal requests for affiliate earnings.\n- [Admin Verify KYC](../admin/verify-kyc) — Admin queue for reviewing submitted KYC applications.\n",
  "settings/workspace": "# Workspace & Team Settings\n\nConfigure organization identity, workspace display name, default timezones, and team member permission tiers.\n\n> **View in Application →** [Open Workspace Settings](/dashboard/settings/workspace)\n\n![Screenshot placeholder: Workspace Settings](./images/settings-workspace.png)\n> **Screenshot:** Workspace Settings page showing workspace name editor, team size limits, plan tier indicators, and organization preferences.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Workspace Settings tab allows you to organize your business workspace. Whether you are an individual creator or an agency managing social commerce for multiple brands, your workspace holds your team credentials, settings, and business profile.\n\n## What You Can Do\n\n- Update your Workspace Display Name.\n- Review your current plan tier's Team Size Limit (e.g., 5 member seats on Creator Pro).\n- Configure default workspace timezones for accurate post scheduling.\n- Save organization branding preferences.\n\n## How to Use\n\n### Step 1: Open Workspace Settings\nNavigate to **Settings > Workspace** from the main sidebar.\n\n### Step 2: Edit Workspace Details\n1. Update your **Workspace Name** (e.g., *\"Alex Rivera Media Studio\"*).\n2. Review your team seat allocation.\n3. Click **Save Settings** to confirm.\n\n## Available Workspace Options\n\n| Option / Setting | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Workspace Name** | Organization or business name displayed in navigation headers and invoices. |\n| **Team Size Limit** | Maximum team member seats supported under your active subscription plan. |\n| **Plan Status** | Shows active plan tier (Free Trial or Creator Pro). |\n\n## Related Features\n\n- [Connected Accounts](./accounts) — Link social media accounts to this workspace.\n- [AI Agent Configuration](./ai) — Customize AI business knowledge and responses for this workspace.\n"
};
